"winningTimeRankDir":5,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"menRecords":["overall"],"menPreviousRecord":{"time":"05:27:18","holder":"Bruce FORDYCE","year":1984,"type":"overall"},"heroicSecond":{"name":"Bob DE LA MOTTE","time":"05:26:12","athleteId":"CBB2B390-7EDE-4039-B8F4-BD689D4713FC","brokenRecord":{"time":"05:27:18","holder":"Bruce FORDYCE","year":1984,"type":"overall"}},"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1952,"mensWinner":"Trevor ALLEN","mensTime":"07:00:02"}},"narrative":"The 1986 Comrades Marathon was the 61st running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 88.771 km. The race was held on Saturday, 31 May. Conditions: Clear and cool at start. Mild to warm later. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nBruce FORDYCE claimed the men's title in 05:24:07, ahead of Bob DE LA MOTTE (05:26:12) and Hoseah TJALE (05:29:02). Helen LUCRE won the women's race in 06:55:01, followed by Ralie SMIT (07:07:40).\n\nBruce FORDYCE's 05:24:07 broke FORDYCE's own course record of 05:27:18 set in 1984. Remarkably, runner-up Bob DE LA MOTTE's 05:26:12 also beat the previous record of 05:27:18 — a rare feat in Comrades history. Helen LUCRE's 06:55:01 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1952 (Trevor ALLEN, 07:00:02).\n\nFrom a field of 11,443 entries, 9,651 runners crossed the finish line (84.3% completion rate), with athletes representing over 18 countries. The field comprised 9,219 men and 432 women (4.5% female). The average finish time was 09:14:19.\n\nMedals awarded: 11 Gold, 1,195 Silver, 8,445 Bronze. 3,598 runners (37.3%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Hugh COTTRELL in 11:00:00.\n\nThis edition featured the 5th fastest winning time on record. Compared to the previous down run in 1984, the field was 61.1% larger.","countryDataPct":100.0}